@kubernetes/sig-testing any idea why the ign file loaded from: `/workspace/test-infra/jobs/e2e_node/crio/crio_cgrpv2_k8s_infra_prow_build.ign` does not correspond to the current master version of test-infra? 

In particular, the parsed version of the file (see the logs here: https://storage.googleapis.com/kubernetes-jenkins/pr-logs/pull/113205/pull-kubernetes-node-crio-cgrpv2-e2e-kubetest2/1625146348607115264/artifacts/build-log.txt) contains the `a8c9ddc773007c61074e224bd740ca3aecd7fecb` pointer to the version of CRIO to use for testing, whereas the master version (see here: https://github.com/kubernetes/test-infra/blob/master/jobs/e2e_node/crio/crio_cgrpv2_k8s_infra_prow_build.ign) is pointing to `fa0d058141343ee38b8339ea41f580c361271372`.

This appears to be an issue only with the `kubetest2` tests. For example the analogous test (but without `-kubetest2`) gets the master version of the file. See in the logs: https://storage.googleapis.com/kubernetes-jenkins/pr-logs/pull/113205/pull-kubernetes-node-crio-cgrpv2-e2e/1625055986949558272/build-log.txt.
